@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:security] public-repository-credentials
Credentials MUST stay outside tracked source and MUST NOT appear in logs, artifacts, prompts or
exceptions. Provider credentials are loaded from the ignored environment or CI secret store.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:safety] guarded-native-work
Unreal and Blender work MUST use Atelier's existing lock and actual-child memory guard. No code
may bypass admission, signal another owner's process or share mutable generated folders between
checkouts. A capacity plan is advisory until a separately validated admission service replaces it.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] paid-call-provenance
Every paid operation MUST have an exclusive ledger record before submission and a terminal or
uncertain record afterward. An uncertain operation MUST NOT be retried automatically.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:architecture] platform-game-boundary
Platform modules MUST NOT name a particular game. Game-specific recipes, assets and runtime
behavior belong under games/<game>; reusable mechanisms belong under platform/.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:architecture] fork-import-cleanliness
Code ported from contributor forks MUST conform to upstream ownership and build rules before
merge. Committed assets under games/<game>/assets/ MUST remain immutable inputs and MUST NOT be
overwritten in place by carving or baking scripts or duplicated into shadow backup folders.
Derived meshes and materials MUST be produced under build/<game>/ or unreal/Content/ by the
owning build steps with bounded triangle counts and LODs, and runtime consumers MUST share
existing domain tables and authored placement transforms rather than duplicating them in C++.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] contract-review-before-merge
Every PR MUST check contract syntax/owners and review applicable contracts on its final code.
Review findings are advisory: an agent MAY resolve a false positive with a recorded explanation.
Contract checks MUST NOT be installed as required merge gates. Syntax checks alone MUST NOT be
presented as proof of semantic compliance. All contract owners MUST be fontanierh.
